From: lisa build kit <dev@local>
Subject: [PATCH] camera2: hide virtual aux camera IDs from non-whitelisted apps

Ports the Xiaomi/Qualcomm behaviour found in HyperOS OS2.0.8.0.UKOMIXM
(lisa): virtual cameras (IDs 5 and 6 on lisa) are only exposed to
packages listed in vendor.camera.aux.packagelist (e.g. the MiuiCamera
package com.android.camera). Other apps get a filtered camera ID list
and no longer crash with "do not support any formats" when opening them.

The stock Qualcomm behaviour truncated the list to the first two map
entries (i == 2), which would also hide the real front camera; this
patch instead skips only the IDs from vendor.camera.aux.hiddenids
(default "5,6"), so all real cameras stay visible to every app.

Requires the device tree to set in vendor.prop:
    vendor.camera.aux.packagelist=com.android.camera
Without that property the behaviour is unchanged (all IDs exposed).

---
--- a/core/java/android/hardware/camera2/CameraManager.java	2026-11-05 10:32:05.855520800 -0800
+++ b/core/java/android/hardware/camera2/CameraManager.java	2026-11-05 10:32:05.949520900 -0800
@@ -2487,8 +2487,8 @@
             try {
                 List<String> cameraIds = new ArrayList<>();
                 boolean exposeAuxCamera = Camera.shouldExposeAuxCamera();
+                Set<String> hiddenAuxCameraIds = getHiddenAuxCameraIds(exposeAuxCamera);
                 for (int i = 0; i < mDeviceStatus.size(); i++) {
-                    if (!exposeAuxCamera && i == 2) break;
                     int status = mDeviceStatus.valueAt(i);
                     DeviceCameraInfo info = mDeviceStatus.keyAt(i);
                     if (status == ICameraServiceListener.STATUS_NOT_PRESENT
@@ -2496,6 +2496,9 @@
                             || shouldHideCamera(deviceId, devicePolicy, info)) {
                         continue;
                     }
+                    if (hiddenAuxCameraIds.contains(info.mCameraId)) {
+                        continue;
+                    }
                     cameraIds.add(info.mCameraId);
                 }
                 return cameraIds.toArray(new String[0]);
@@ -2507,6 +2510,23 @@
             }
         }
 
+        /**
+         * Virtual/auxiliary camera IDs hidden from apps that are not whitelisted
+         * via vendor.camera.aux.packagelist (Xiaomi-style aux camera filtering).
+         * Configured through vendor.camera.aux.hiddenids, default "5,6" for lisa.
+         */
+        private static Set<String> getHiddenAuxCameraIds(boolean exposeAuxCamera) {
+            Set<String> hidden = new ArraySet<>();
+            if (exposeAuxCamera) {
+                return hidden;
+            }
+            String ids = SystemProperties.get("vendor.camera.aux.hiddenids", "5,6");
+            for (String id : ids.split(",")) {
+                hidden.add(id.trim());
+            }
+            return hidden;
+        }
+
         private Set<Set<String>> extractConcurrentCameraIdListLocked(int deviceId,
                 int devicePolicy) {
             Set<Set<String>> concurrentCameraIds = new ArraySet<>();
